#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115390 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/id #uuid "ce098ff9-2ef1-5483-b057-b3fef12af16d" :question/math-academy-id "e-2477" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532910 :question-generator/id #uuid "34f2c402-acc1-5020-9544-72c94be0f985" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115390.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "245c1016-9019-52b2-a26a-6ac0bf1d16f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302689} {:answer/id #uuid "3f808494-9cca-5881-91d6-e03f7e4beb4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302855} {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc6f526-3686-5eb6-a589-7d892e3678c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303726} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d545bc-df18-5895-b155-25b6a18a659c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25a159b-0633-5804-97a2-dac583cb6e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303644} :answer-field/id #uuid "41acddb3-3570-5655-ad47-cf8c72851a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17db3926-f364-5101-a69e-c1d34df6ed10" :question/math-academy-id "q-33122" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad37ff22-26f6-50cd-9218-b742d80d0369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8, 1,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113623} {:answer/id #uuid "dce955db-803a-5eaa-8f40-9514713111b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 0, 48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113624} {:answer/id #uuid "51ccd42e-d655-5177-a52d-935b7434f13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24, 3, 36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113625} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3be7aa-7f8b-5864-bdec-850462bcfb32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6, 0, 24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113626} {:answer/id #uuid "7a69da90-0384-583a-882a-0121d8fd94a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12, 3,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113627}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2b7ff49b-47bd-5f8b-a647-fae948868913" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113622}] :question/id #uuid "a73b3659-30e4-5063-9479-5d3e2f941065" :question/math-academy-id "q-33143" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$h(t)|= ⟨2t^{2}, t - 3, 8 + t^{3}⟩; g(t)|= ⟨t^{2} + 2t, 8, 2t^{3}⟩$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b40cf7a-fa7c-5050-b2e9-e2f7ba04828a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259977} {:answer/id #uuid "175264bb-f389-5869-951c-76cc68611d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260079} {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} {:answer/id #uuid "395164b8-31dd-524a-ab0d-565231ea5e45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260386} {:answer/id #uuid "fce4134e-0fcd-5135-8ad0-7457cadd83ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "214e0a46-a997-57f6-8fa7-46beb9676f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260159} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eac5ff3-a989-52ce-a1dc-128ad336dc00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65ab200e-3546-5bdf-91aa-8c6105b3b769" :question/math-academy-id "q-128137" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}$ at $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3(t+1)},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-3{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3(t+1)}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(0)-3g(0))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(0)-3{g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+1}},\\,3(0)^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{0+1}⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3(0+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e9deaa-32e1-5ea1-8ac9-d0b7cec610d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260804} {:answer/id #uuid "786ded6e-e2cc-5b48-8f31-f18de453ddf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260928} {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} {:answer/id #uuid "bee221f3-f2b6-59f9-bc02-f014daed57c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\pi ,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261564} {:answer/id #uuid "e98af580-cfca-5b9f-a49f-53c6b11bb2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,4\\pi ,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "925c6509-691b-597c-8503-36e96b674fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261146} :answer-field/id #uuid "04f0cbd8-ad26-5506-89ef-79e23f60a2f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d61cd968-7256-5d6b-88d3-edf46ce0ae3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128452" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}$ at $t=-1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨8\\sqrt{3-t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}-t,\\,\\pi {t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(2f(t)-g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)-{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8\\sqrt{3-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-t}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-1,\\,2\\pi t,\\,-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(-1)-g(-1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(-1)-{g}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3-(-1)}},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi ),\\,\\frac{1}{(-1)}⟩-⟨2(-1)-1,\\,2\\pi (-1),\\,-2(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-2,-\\pi ,-1⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2\\pi ,-2⟩-⟨-3,-2\\pi ,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f2fbae0-f6d7-546c-827c-374938408879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260853} {:answer/id #uuid "71402034-ff9c-5e89-8506-730d8d44e9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260867} {:answer/id #uuid "92984806-47e0-5523-b871-7b33717a7972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261148} {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} {:answer/id #uuid "fc50c87f-1bce-55e7-87f1-cf2d24533ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d34e1c49-8247-5b18-a5d2-f237fc07b65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261733} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a5d268-0bb4-5a51-b597-b06cd810f718" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "143a675a-6cf0-552b-b195-46b4f34bf0d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128458" :question/problem "Find the value of $(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{3+t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2t-3 \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ (t+1)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have \n \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+5g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+5{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(2\\sqrt{3+t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+t}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+1)^{2})\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 2(t+1)\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence , we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(1)+5g(1))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(1)+5{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1-1) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2(1) \\\\ 2(1+1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6f401a-1af1-5902-8ecf-8f185e9e12da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300092} {:answer/id #uuid "3d489b9a-c7ce-5bb5-9c1e-bb2fb01f89fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300261} {:answer/id #uuid "7630cb27-95dd-503c-86cf-d9a96b47156b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300546} {:answer/id #uuid "875ea830-aed4-554d-85ae-d63a3f76be32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ef80ee-161a-5a7e-8232-8f11f4ab0591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299960} :answer-field/id #uuid "610d999b-36f3-554e-acdc-7690f0627a2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ce8c747-438b-5a4a-8cfe-ec69b8a216ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-32499" :question/problem "Differentiate $2g(t)-h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3t-3,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-t,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have\n\n$$\n(2g(t)-h(t))^{′}=2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2g(t)-h(t))^{′} & =2{g}^{′}(t)-{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3,\\,-2t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6,\\,-4t⟩-⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6-(-1),\\,-4t-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,7,\\,-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2a4bfc-5f35-5ae9-a821-d3bce3a9c6c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300442} {:answer/id #uuid "7a714d86-ceb0-57c7-a902-31a1b72e5f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300565} {:answer/id #uuid "87911319-25bb-5038-bd99-46da453974fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t-1,0,t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300646} {:answer/id #uuid "9e03f1e2-6fb5-5862-a16d-73e44a1f2e33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2t+1,2t+1,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31df8d49-ce69-5cb1-a2cd-57e59e1196c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2t-1,0,2t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300209} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4e2c0bf-91fb-53b7-a114-172b95036f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f67b45fc-cd86-5ee0-8299-de9e4060f565" :question/math-academy-id "q-32503" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)+h(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨-t,\\,0,t⟩ \\\\ h(t) & =⟨-{t}^{2},0,{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ {h}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t)+h(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)+{h}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩+⟨-1,0,1⟩+⟨-2t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t-1,\\,0,\\,2t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41126a54-8e43-5888-909a-644b0fa2584e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302866} {:answer/id #uuid "89b704e5-d1d6-5b5f-b7c9-5e1091541afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303316} {:answer/id #uuid "989a417c-9f9c-520c-a1ca-b762a6d26b64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303404} {:answer/id #uuid "a7aa4261-f293-5497-8bca-0be34ef4c95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303485} {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e704354b-3077-58df-9da8-1fc39413f08b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303892} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb6aef3-3384-522e-8f0d-b00fdf0b7619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3147421-0af0-52d2-8626-d7432dc16238" :question/math-academy-id "q-33123" :question/problem "Differentiate $2f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,(j-\\,k) \\\\ g(t) & =(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and the sum rules, we have \n\n$$\n(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′}=2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}1\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+3g(t))^{′} & =2{f}^{′}(t)+3{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)+3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ti-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac5b001-3222-5f20-9cfa-a6a178edbcf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336134} {:answer/id #uuid "43211d42-ef9b-5294-9784-f61afc4354fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336665} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0b1790-c755-5de3-8e68-28d3776dc12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336737} {:answer/id #uuid "adc3c998-c9bf-5aa6-bbfb-3bb4b5b897c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337591} {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d10a81b8-09d6-54a4-86e1-fa3b6c978c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337863} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a6a4498-4274-5a8f-a340-b4c6887cef4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bba82f4d-eee0-52ff-96d4-e8a4604b03f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70681" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a768cdba-762c-56fa-9c5a-e7c147a0278c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387861} {:answer/id #uuid "308ec3e7-64ed-53d8-95f6-4019058929dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387862} {:answer/id #uuid "c6683669-2c03-5f5d-9b0c-ade45ed8142d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387863} {:answer/id #uuid "76309ab8-5db5-5655-9fd2-0aa6a5daad69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387864} {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3051e681-37d6-5351-a17b-b57925e0ca74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387865} :answer-field/id #uuid "437f6985-a5fd-5604-8d5e-718379fa984b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e49dfe3-04a3-591e-9ea0-48737f115840" :question/math-academy-id "q-127998" :question/problem "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a16c9dc1-0124-53fd-9b82-d496e53dbcff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387868} {:answer/id #uuid "f616ca61-be0f-5144-b6c8-08476269dd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387869} {:answer/id #uuid "309785b0-a118-5c93-829d-4b1bec8533d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,7,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387870} {:answer/id #uuid "a99725fb-c5ed-5e02-9f65-da1970e78632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,7,9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387871} {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69eaec62-e0f1-50fe-ae12-fb1a693cb8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-5,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387872} :answer-field/id #uuid "f682f616-b62a-5bba-8f73-0577cd6f697d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "998ff16d-b6a6-5973-8b01-9ee14eef7c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-128144" :question/problem "Find the value of $(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-2{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(1)-2g(1))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(1)-2{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =⟨2(1),\\,\\frac{1}{1},\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩-2⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}},\\,3(1)^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-2⟨1,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141f5551-934e-5440-8953-1b3d3cf88e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,i+12 e^{4 t}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532866} {:answer/id #uuid "44aab5b3-a627-5319-b75d-247ebb8b0162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6 - 9 t^{2})\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} - \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532874} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6b1f0d-8766-51a0-9b69-2576acc19597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3 t^{3} + 6 t + 3)\\,i+\\frac{3 \\left(\\left(t + 2\\right) e^{4 t} - 1\\right)}{t + 2}\\,j+6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532879} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2d1687-1eb8-5477-9fad-53c4f1a5c47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532897} {:answer/id #uuid "fa448647-c439-5d87-9345-4f25b8d6061c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb2d1687-1eb8-5477-9fad-53c4f1a5c47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532897} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b16c366-2ff9-5f7d-bf99-55f090fe22ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0ea031d4-a7c9-52a4-913c-d764f5dca240" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $3f(t)+3g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(t^{3} + 2)\\,i- \\frac{1}{t + 2}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(2 t - 1)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3f(t)+3g(t))'=3f'(\\!t)+3g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{3} + 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- \\frac{1}{t + 2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=3 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=2\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3f(t)+3g(t))'&=3f'(\\!t)+3g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=3\\left(3 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+3\\left(2\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(6\\,i+12 e^{4 t}\\,j- 9 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(9 t^{2} + 6)\\,i+(12 e^{4 t} + \\frac{3}{\\left(t + 2\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 18 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e97975-4c74-5507-b653-606d0d1bf2e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532868} {:answer/id #uuid "66c548d2-02d8-5526-b8e1-1c99ae671173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532880} {:answer/id #uuid "86ed3a70-cdde-56de-b810-9899566e914d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532887} {:answer/id #uuid "eed0e2f3-ee96-5a6d-a583-fb4c12616f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 8 t^{2} + 2 t - 10)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t - 3\\right) e^{4 t} + 4\\right)}{t - 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532906} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7037f7-a559-5d3e-be45-91f41c699e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16 t + 2)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66c548d2-02d8-5526-b8e1-1c99ae671173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532880} :answer-field/id #uuid "468a0c5a-ad2b-5b7f-abac-b961a5396963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20b4dae3-6b9d-5ae1-bd0a-7100a3030dee" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(4 t^{2} + 1)\\,i- \\frac{4}{t - 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(t - 4)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t^{2} + 1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- \\frac{4}{t - 3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=1\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(1\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(2\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(2 - 16 t)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t - 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105fc45b-d9aa-5647-8478-24ee897554e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532865} {:answer/id #uuid "a392fa70-156d-57e7-82f2-0893b7b7ab65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-108,\\,3,\\,-252⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532892} {:answer/id #uuid "c18dca8f-f976-58fb-937e-0955da836ca5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24,\\,19,\\,48⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532900} {:answer/id #uuid "d09c0c53-ad7d-5a79-92c3-cda91d610220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-36,\\,0,\\,-144⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532902} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d46704-3cf7-544d-aa5b-932780b205a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨72,\\,-3,\\,108⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105fc45b-d9aa-5647-8478-24ee897554e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532865} :answer-field/id #uuid "230e9f4b-ec6e-5a43-aa1f-9d2f50c7feb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "531c6c00-7c33-51fe-bcdf-6ff4d87bd71d" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$h(t)= ⟨6 t^{2},\\,3 - t,\\,3 t^{3} + 24⟩; g(t)= ⟨3 t \\left(t + 2\\right),\\,-8,\\,6 t^{3}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3h(t)-2g(t))'=3h'(\\!t)-2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6 t^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 - t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 24)⟩ \\\\ &=⟨12 t,\\,-1,\\,9 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t \\left(t + 2\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-8),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6 t^{3})⟩ \\\\ &=⟨6 t + 6,\\,0,\\,18 t^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3h(t)-2g(t))'\\big|_{t=2}&=3h'(\\!2)-2g'(\\!2) \\\\ &=3\\left(⟨24,\\,-1,\\,36⟩\\right)-2\\left(⟨18,\\,0,\\,72⟩\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(⟨72,\\,-3,\\,108⟩\\right)+\\left(⟨-36,\\,0,\\,-144⟩\\right) \\\\ &=⟨36,\\,-3,\\,-36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f3c848-dbff-5f1b-ad1b-23f4831d8ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532862} {:answer/id #uuid "0c89cfd6-cb3c-558c-a04b-8bfe30bf8644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨24,\\,-9,\\,-72⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532863} {:answer/id #uuid "19302086-6cf1-5118-9c0d-909000840d68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,0,\\,96⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532867} {:answer/id #uuid "5aea8fe7-71be-55cc-b3e6-e7535c8fb3b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,\\,57,\\,-32⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532878} {:answer/id #uuid "eec84841-0dae-5761-b467-ce2eb2342da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-36,\\,9,\\,168⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07f3c848-dbff-5f1b-ad1b-23f4831d8ffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532862} :answer-field/id #uuid "7288ecef-567e-595a-b90c-71125b365b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a68d13f-8399-5ff1-b774-b1b84a373282" :question/problem "Find the value of $(3h(t) - 2g(t))^{′}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$h(t)= ⟨2 t^{2},\\,9 - 3 t,\\,- 2 t^{3} - 16⟩; g(t)= ⟨t \\left(t + 2\\right),\\,-24,\\,- 4 t^{3}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(3h(t)-2g(t))'=3h'(\\!t)-2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9 - 3 t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t^{3} - 16)⟩ \\\\ &=⟨4 t,\\,-3,\\,- 6 t^{2}⟩ \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\left(t + 2\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-24),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t^{3})⟩ \\\\ &=⟨2 t + 2,\\,0,\\,- 12 t^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3h(t)-2g(t))'\\big|_{t=2}&=3h'(\\!2)-2g'(\\!2) \\\\ &=3\\left(⟨8,\\,-3,\\,-24⟩\\right)-2\\left(⟨6,\\,0,\\,-48⟩\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(⟨24,\\,-9,\\,-72⟩\\right)+\\left(⟨-12,\\,0,\\,96⟩\\right) \\\\ &=⟨12,\\,-9,\\,24⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2592c444-2abd-56c3-9730-56a494189a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532872} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f57fdd-7ab8-5ee9-bfdd-4e1c04109c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532893} {:answer/id #uuid "aa480904-ff84-518d-9207-ac8579b1dfa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 12 t^{2})\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} - \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532894} {:answer/id #uuid "abcbc025-80ba-5616-8a44-cda642191303" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 t^{3} + 8 t + 4)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t - 1\\right) e^{4 t} - 2\\right)}{t - 1}\\,j+4 \\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532895} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5d88ac-cf94-5f91-89c9-923fa247b61f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9f57fdd-7ab8-5ee9-bfdd-4e1c04109c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532893} :answer-field/id #uuid "93b0a0f6-d902-5422-9a0c-2f37556f6f7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "709685a4-0960-5ef6-9050-4e687533ef07" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(2 t^{3} + 4)\\,i- \\frac{2}{t - 1}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(4 t - 2)\\,i+e^{4 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(2f(t)+2g(t))'=2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{3} + 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- \\frac{2}{t - 1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=6 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t - 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{4 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=4\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2f(t)+2g(t))'&=2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=2\\left(6 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(4\\,i+4 e^{4 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(12 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(8\\,i+8 e^{4 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(12 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(8 e^{4 t} + \\frac{4}{\\left(t - 1\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05042b03-df4c-5ccd-a964-8eaf6131a969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532861} {:answer/id #uuid "1c3aff9f-c826-5930-ba16-3983961fdd31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532869} {:answer/id #uuid "838a64ec-997e-5f8b-96bd-2d63e5eac034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 t^{2}\\,i- \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532885} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0d38a-bfd3-57c3-907f-f60c0eb825dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 6 t^{3} + 8 t - 14)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t + 3\\right) e^{2 t} + 3\\right)}{t + 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532890} {:answer/id #uuid "bf993974-3b0c-5c9f-886d-1d6ca421c69c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18 t^{2} + 8)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} + \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 16 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c3aff9f-c826-5930-ba16-3983961fdd31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532869} :answer-field/id #uuid "f573ff47-df7f-5224-8ed0-621e1426dd66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8facb5d0-2042-58b2-9944-895664b71392" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(3 t^{3} + 4)\\,i- \\frac{3}{t + 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(4 t - 3)\\,i+e^{2 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t^{3} + 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- \\frac{3}{t + 3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t - 3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(4 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=4\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(9 t^{2}\\,i+\\frac{3}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(4\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 18 t^{2}\\,i- \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(8\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 8 \\sin{\\left(4 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(8 - 18 t^{2})\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{6}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49b54258-61d2-549c-94e4-a251f6d2a656" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "777522b1-6939-5b66-8d41-4c0af7a31559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532884} {:answer/id #uuid "8631399e-befe-5fda-89cf-04216c222ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532886} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ccd2c1-ee5e-53ce-8fa5-271cd400ba26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 8 t^{2} + 4 t - 12)\\,i+\\frac{2 \\left(\\left(t + 3\\right) e^{2 t} + 4\\right)}{t + 3}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532896} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9aa792-0b2d-537e-877a-bee6cb6606f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(16 t + 4)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} + \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j- 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532898} {:answer/id #uuid "dd248600-23aa-53ba-92c5-dd1baf90dce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8631399e-befe-5fda-89cf-04216c222ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532886} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e314097-0298-520f-9c83-0f0fe71e1ac1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2b09545-4d92-5fd4-a34e-ae79048ac39c" :question/problem "Find the derivative of $-2f(t)+2g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=(4 t^{2} + 2)\\,i- \\frac{4}{t + 3}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g(t)&=(2 t - 4)\\,i+e^{2 t}\\,j+\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(-2f(t)+2g(t))'=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4 t^{2} + 2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- \\frac{4}{t + 3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k \\\\ g'(t)&=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})⟩ \\\\ &=2\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2f(t)+2g(t))'&=-2f'(\\!t)+2g'(\\!t) \\\\ &=-2\\left(8 t\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+2\\left(2\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j- 3 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(- 16 t\\,i- \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}}\\,j+6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right)+\\left(4\\,i+4 e^{2 t}\\,j- 6 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\,k\\right) \\\\ &=(4 - 16 t)\\,i+(4 e^{2 t} - \\frac{8}{\\left(t + 3\\right)^{2}})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules for Differentiation"}]}
